# Frontend env examples for Vite
# Save a copy to `frontend/.env` and restart dev server after editing.

# During local dev, Vite dev server can proxy `/api` to your backend.
# Set the proxy target (used by `vite.config.ts`) to your backend address:
VITE_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:4000

# For production or when calling a remote backend directly from the browser,
# set the absolute API base URL. If set, the app will call `${VITE_API_BASE}/api/...`.
# Example (Codespaces forwarded public URL for the server):
# VITE_API_BASE=https://fictional-robot-5g5gjwrg7v3vq7j-4000.app.github.dev
VITE_API_BASE=
